    "description": "Reps must be able to create and customize their OWN (private) list views, but must not be able to edit, rename, delete, or re-share any list view that is public or shared with them (including the standard \"All\" / \"Recently Viewed\" views and the curated Console views).\n\nBuild:\n\n* Remove \"Manage Public List Views\" from the Rep profile and the Rep permission set group (see BUILD-01 / BUILD-26 for the 4-tier PSG).\n\n* Verify across all Console objects: Sign_Up\\__c, Deal_Rep_Assignmentc, Dealc, Account (Player/Referrer/Operator/Partner RTs), Study_Link_Click_\\_c.\n\n* Regression-test that reps can still create a private list view and edit their own filters/columns.\n\n* Confirm the curated Console views (BUILD-17, BUILD-37, BUILD-48) are owned by an admin/integration user, not by a rep — a rep who CREATED a shared view can still edit it.\n\nConstraints / caveats to call out at review:\n\n* \"Manage Public List Views\" is an org-wide user permission, not per-object. Removing it applies to every object the rep can see — that is the desired outcome here, but there is no granular per-object option.\n\n* Reps also lose the ability to create list views visible to others. Intentional.\n\n* Any list view currently owned by a rep will need reassignment before this bites.\n\nEffort: \\~2-3h incl. cross-object testing.\n\nSource: Kobi, 2026-08-05.",
